response.answer:
Simply put, BCIT must confirm:

- whether your education and English qualifications are acceptable;
- whether your questionnaire, references, and any credential assessment meet requirements;
- whether you’re selected through competitive admission.

IRCC—not BCIT—makes final study-permit and post-graduation work-permit decisions.

[Program details](https://www.bcit.ca/programs/applied-computing-master-of-science-full-time-m600msc/)

